auth {
  mode: none
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
}

script:pre-request {
  // Binance "MARKET_DATA" endpoints (e.g. old trades lookup) require the
  // X-MBX-APIKEY header but no request signature. The header is ignored by
  // fully public endpoints, so when an apiKey is configured in the active
  // environment it is simply sent on every request.
  const apiKey = bru.getEnvVar('apiKey');
  if (apiKey) {
    req.setHeader('X-MBX-APIKEY', apiKey);
  }
}

docs {
  # Binance Options REST API — public market data

  A Bruno collection covering the public (unauthenticated) REST endpoints in
  **Market Data**, generated from the official Binance Postman collection
  (binance/binance-api-postman).

  ## Setup

  1. Select an environment (see environments/).
  2. No credentials are needed for public endpoints. Endpoints marked
     MARKET_DATA additionally require an API key: set the `apiKey` secret
     environment variable and the collection pre-request script sends it as
     the X-MBX-APIKEY header automatically. No endpoint here needs signing.

  Base URLs:
  - production: https://eapi.binance.com

  References:
  - https://developers.binance.com/docs/derivatives/option/market-data
  Changelog: https://developers.binance.com/en/docs/products/spot/CHANGELOG
}
